# Fitness Tracking App with Location Tracking

I'll build this as a **React Native (Expo)** app, since it works on iOS and Android. It records GPS routes, distance, pace, and duration, and saves workouts.

## 1. Setup

```bash
npx create-expo-app FitTrack
cd FitTrack
npx expo install expo-location react-native-maps @react-native-async-storage/async-storage expo-task-manager
```

## 2. `app.json` (permissions)

```json
{
  "expo": {
    "name": "FitTrack",
    "slug": "fittrack",
    "ios": {
      "infoPlist": {
        "NSLocationWhenInUseUsageDescription": "FitTrack uses your location to record your workout route.",
        "NSLocationAlwaysAndWhenInUseUsageDescription": "FitTrack tracks your route during workouts, even in the background.",
        "UIBackgroundModes": ["location"]
      }
    },
    "android": {
      "permissions": [
        "ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION",
        "ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION",
        "ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION",
        "FOREGROUND_SERVICE",
        "FOREGROUND_SERVICE_LOCATION"
      ]
    },
    "plugins": [
      ["expo-location", {
        "isAndroidBackgroundLocationEnabled": true,
        "isIosBackgroundLocationEnabled": true
      }]
    ]
  }
}
```

